  "reason": "The study compares different metrics (IC10 vs IC50) for predicting QT prolongation in humans based on in vitro hERG inhibition data. While it discusses prediction and discrimination (AUC), it does not report a quantitative measure of agreement between non-human animal results and human clinical results. The comparison is between different in vitro measures and their predictive power for human outcomes, not a direct comparison of animal model concordance with human clinical results."
